# Web frontend structure

## Layout
- Routes live under `apps/web/src/pages/<route>/` (URL-mirrored folders). Domains **never** contain `pages/`.
- Thin pages render domain `*Panel` components under `domains/<domain>/components/`.
- Providers stay in `src/app/providers/`. `AppRouter` reads `src/config/routes.config.tsx`.
- Cross-cutting HTTP helpers stay in `src/lib/`.

## Domains may contain
`components/`, `hooks/`, `interfaces/`, `constants/`, `services/`, `helpers/` — create a folder only when a file lands. Prefer `helpers/` over `utils/`.

## Naming
- UI props / view models: `*.interface.ts` under `interfaces/`.
- TypeScript `enum` values: `*.constant.ts` under `constants/` (file says constant; use `enum`). Do **not** put helper functions in constant files.
- Pure helpers: `*.helper.ts` under `helpers/` (domain) or `src/lib/helpers/` (cross-domain).
- One file = one responsibility. Split list UIs into `*List` / `*ListItem` / `*ListItemActions`.
- Do **not** duplicate Orval/OpenAPI DTOs; import from `@bookmark-manager/api-client`.
- Reuse shared `Loading`, `NoData`, and alert/toast — do not copy loading/empty Typography into every screen.
- Access failures navigate to `/403` or `/404` pages (API privacy not-invited → `/404`); do not inline not-found/forbidden trees in every screen.

## Config
- `src/config/routes.config.tsx` — `{ path, element, requireAuth, layout }`
- `src/config/features.config.ts` — feature toggles
- Layout chrome is `src/app/App.tsx` (`<App />`), not AppShell
- UI copy stays inline in components/screens — do **not** add a labels/i18n config
- Public URLs must not change without an explicit Auth0 + docs update (`/callback` stays `/callback`).
